; Values (docs/foundations.md, Stage 2): literals, truths, printing, equals.
; Numbers print in canonical form, which reads back as an equal number.
0
-0
-7
10/4
-9/5
18446744073709551614/2
1/9223372036854775807
true
false
; equals: numbers exactly, whatever the spelling
2/3 equals 4/6
2/3 equals 1/3
-0 equals 0
5 equals 10/2
-9/5 equals -18/10
; truths by truth value
true equals true
true equals false
; different kinds are unequal, even when they look alike
5 equals true
1 equals true
; protos by identity: an alias is the same proto
dog is a world
pet is dog
dog equals pet
; two protos with the same parent and the same teaching are still two
rex is a dog
fido is a dog
rex ask sound is 1
fido ask sound is 1
rex equals fido
rex equals dog
dog equals 5
; truth literals are the truth values the language already has
c is a world
t is c inherits world
t equals true
t and true
false or t
; printing reads back: the printed value, read again, is equal
n is 18/10
n
9/5 equals n
